--- 

This guide assumes that you are already familiar with Neovims built-in package manager [Pack](https://neovim.io/doc/user/pack/), [nvim-lspconfig](https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig) and [nvim-treesitter](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter).

Prerequisites are that you have [SuperHTML](https://github.com/kristoff-it/superhtml) and [Ziggy](https://github.com/kristoff-it/ziggy) installed and available in your `$PATH`.

The following is a complete Neovim configuration that:
- installs `nvim-lspconfig` and `nvim-treesitter` plugins using Neovim's built-in plugin manager;
- enables the usage of SuperHTML, Ziggy and Ziggy Schema language servers;
- and installs the corresponding Tree-sitter parser.

```lua
vim.pack.add{
  { src = 'https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig' },
  { src = 'https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter' }
}

vim.lsp.enable('superhtml')
vim.lsp.enable('ziggy')
vim.lsp.enable('ziggy_schema')

require('nvim-treesitter').install({ 'superhtml', 'ziggy', 'ziggy_schema' })
```

The Tree-sitter parsers for SuperMD are not yet available via `nvim-treesitter`.
To install and enable them use following snipped based on the [official `nvim-treesitter` documentation](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter#adding-custom-languages):

```lua
vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'TSUpdate',
callback = function()
  require('nvim-treesitter.parsers').supermd = {
    install_info = {
      url = 'https://github.com/kristoff-it/supermd',
      location = 'tree-sitter/supermd',
    },
	}
  require('nvim-treesitter.parsers').supermd_inline = {
    install_info = {
      url = 'https://github.com/kristoff-it/supermd',
      location = 'tree-sitter/supermd-inline',
    },
	}
end})

require('nvim-treesitter').install { 'supermd', 'supermd_inline' }
```
